      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hong%C5%8D%2C_Tokyo",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The University of Tokyo, Japan’s most prestigious university, sits in Hongo’s historic campus.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hong%C5%8D%2C_Tokyo",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Bunkyo Museum, located at 4‑9‑29 Hongo, showcases artifacts from prehistoric Japan to post‑war gadgets.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.gotokyo.org/en/spot/872/index.html",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Hongo’s name comes from Yushima Hongo, meaning the center of Yushima, reflecting its scholarly roots.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.ndl.go.jp/en/landmarks/sights/hongo",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The ruins of the Gojyuden‑mon Gate, a red gate from the 18th‑century Kaga Clan residence, still stand in Hongo.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.ndl.go.jp/en/landmarks/sights/hongo",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Hongo‑sanchome Station, served by the Marunouchi and Toei Oedo Lines, is the main transit hub of the district.",
